		"meta": {
			"author": "Stefan Mazur",
			"category": "source",
			"deploymentTarget": {
				"branch": "",
				"name": "Wire",
				"version": {
					"major": 7,
					"minor": 25,
					"patch": 0
				}
			},
			"description": "Flower Sax - overlay source with alpha: a flat, contour-drawn instrument (Len Lye style) blows flowers out into the room. 'Instrument' selects Saxophone, Trumpet, Snare Drum, Bass Drum, Double Bass or Piano; each has its own starting point and direction. Seven flower kinds (rose, daisy, tulip, blossom, poppy, lily, violet) leave the instrument within a cone of 'Spread' around its direction (360 = in all directions), grow to full size over 'Grow Distance', then fly on independently: moving or turning the instrument only changes where new flowers start. Nothing moves by itself: drive 'Clock' from Arena (Timeline, BPM Sync or FFT +); its rate is the flight speed. If the clock stops, everything stops. 'Scale' sizes everything relative to the output height. Physics: 'Reach' is the flight distance before they fade; 'Fall Strength' with 'Fall Direction' bends the path (where they fall to: 0 = right, 90 = up, 270 = down); 'Tumble' spins the flowers; 'Speed Variation' gives each flower its own speed; 'Depth Spread' spreads them in depth. Flowers: 'Performance Cap' is an upper limit of flowers in flight, for performance only; '<Flower> Count' is a spawn maximum (flowers in flight finish their way, raising it sends new ones out); '<Flower> Color' sets the color of each kind; 'Hue Variation' gives every flower a fixed random hue offset of +\/- that many degrees; 'Hue Shift' turns all flower colors; 'Flower Size' scales the flowers; 'Flowers Opacity' fades them. Instrument: 'Instrument X' \/ 'Instrument Y' move it, 'Instrument Size' scales only the instrument (0 hides it; flowers then start from a single point), 'Instrument Z' pushes instrument and new flowers back (smaller, toward the centre; negative values bring them closer), 'Instrument Rotation' turns it counter-clockwise, 'Instrument Color', 'Line Color', 'Instrument Opacity'. Typical: Rose Count <- Kick, Hue Variation <- Beat, Hue Shift <- Mids. Backdrop On\/Off: On = solid Backdrop Color behind everything, Off = transparent background.",
			"displayName": "Flower Sax",
			"identifier": "4521f53b-bf4b-43ea-a0f0-c59b251b3557",
			"licenseName": "Unlicense",
			"mail": "S.Mazur@cati-co.de",
